Z||000000||Coupe'N||07-12-2001||10:16 PM||||Hey guys/girls, do any of you know what the specs of our electric fans are rated at? I have seen some nice electric fans in the autoparts stores, and wanted to see how ours measure up to them. Also, on a side note, I have adapted my parts cars' fan onto my Ford Ranger. My ranger had a belt driven belt and was robbing around 8-12 horsepower. I MUST be a fiero nut, if I adapt its SOUL into everything I have  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> .<BR>Another thing I have a question about is the little metal bar that is mounted on the fan assembly (84 4 cylinder). The wire (not the ground, but the other one) comes from the fan motor, and goes up to this bar (attaches to a post with a screw) and then exits (same way as it attaches) up to the power source. Anyone know what this piece is? and what does it do?<P>Thanks for any info/help.<BR>Coupe'N outt!!!||||reg||6
Z||000001||FieroSoul||07-13-2001||07:54 PM||||Got one just like it.  You have the HD 2 speed cooling fan. D*#& hard to find if it goes bad. Also D*#$ expensive to replace.  I think my local GM dealer wanted about $275 just for the part.  I bought a used one from Kick Hill for about $35.  Doing fine so far and they are nice to deal with.  The bar is the resistor that causes it to be two speed. ||||reg||1
